invariant: INV-44
file: p384_field.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: p384_field.c keeps its body under a define no build passes, so
  a host object carries the 32-bit field beside the 64-bit one, with
  nothing to call it. test/widemul-builds.sh compiles the file as a
  host object does and requires an object that defines none of its
  routines.

--- old
#ifndef CH_CPU_RUNTIME

#include <string.h>
--- new
#ifndef CH_CPU_HOST

#include <string.h>
